<title>POLAND: POLISH FOOD PRICES RISE 0.2 PCT IN NOV 10-20.</title>
<headline>POLISH FOOD PRICES RISE 0.2 PCT IN NOV 10-20.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food prices rose 0.2</p>
<p>percent in the November 10-20 period after rising 1.8 percent</p>
<p>in the previous 10 days and were two percent higher than in the</p>
<p>October 10-20 period, the Central Statistical Office (GUS)</p>
<p>said.</p>
<p>				  NOV 10-20  NOV  1-10    LAST 30 DAYS</p>
<p>POLISH FOOD PRICES (AVG)	0.2	   1.8	  2.0 (2.0)</p>
<p> Bread				0.3	   0.9	  2.3 (2.2)</p>
<p> Fruit and vegetables	   0.4	  18.5	 18.4 (16.1)</p>
<p> Meat and meat-products	-0.1	  -0.4	 -0.9 (-0.7)</p>
<p> Dairy products		   0.2	   0.4	  0.9 (1.1)</p>
<p> Eggs				 0.5	   1.5	  3.0 (4.4)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets figures for the previous 30-day period</p>
<p>ending on October 20.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
